window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Optimization and Numerical Analysis", "projects": [{"id": "ON-01", "slug": "first-order-convex-optimality", "title": "First-Order Characterization of Convex Minimizers", "level": "Introductory", "idea": "<p>A supporting affine function supplies global sufficiency. Feasible\nline segments supply the converse even when the minimizer is on the\nboundary.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe differentiable and convex, and let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C\\subset\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe nonempty and convex. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nminimizes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nover\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nif and only if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),y-x_*\\rangle\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn particular, on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis is equivalent to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis strictly convex on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthere is at most one minimizer.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Convexity means\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f((1-t)x+ty)\\le(1-t)f(x)+tf(y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le t\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nstrict convexity makes it strict for distinct points and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;t&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nUse differentiation along line segments and the elementary Euclidean\ninner product. This is a characterization at a proposed point, not an\nexistence theorem for arbitrary\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Build the supporting inequality", "role": "<p>Divide the convex secant inequality by its positive parameter and let\nit tend to zero. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x)+\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Differentiable convex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y\\in\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x)+\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The parameter approaches zero through positive values; a one-sided\nsegment is sufficient.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a local Taylor approximation is used as a global lower bound,\nreplace it by this convexity argument; Taylor’s remainder has no\nautomatic sign. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;t\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nconvexity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x+t(y-x))-f(x)\\le t(f(y)-f(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDivide by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Differentiability at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nmakes the left quotient tend to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\downarrow0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRearrangement yields the supporting inequality for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x)+\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Differentiable convex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y\\in\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Divide the convex secant inequality by its positive parameter and let\nit tend to zero.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The parameter approaches zero through positive values; a one-sided\nsegment is sufficient.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Certify constrained optimality", "role": "<p>Use feasible directional derivatives for necessity and the global\nsupport for sufficiency. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a global minimizer over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nexactly when all feasible directional inner products are\nnonnegative.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1, convex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.2.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a global minimizer over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nexactly when all feasible directional inner products are\nnonnegative.</p>", "gate": "<p>A boundary minimizer need not have zero gradient; only feasible\ndirections are tested.</p>", "repair": "<p>If stationarity is imposed at the boundary, restore the\nfeasible-direction inequality instead of demanding all directions have\nzero derivative. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after\na versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nminimizes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe segment\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*+t(y-x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nremains feasible. Its difference quotient from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonnegative for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking the limit gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),y-x_*\\rangle\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Conversely, if those inequalities hold, E1 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x_*)+\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),y-x_*\\rangle\\ge f(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis is the required global conclusion.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a global minimizer over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nexactly when all feasible directional inner products are\nnonnegative.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1, convex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.2. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use feasible directional derivatives for necessity and the global\nsupport for sufficiency.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A boundary minimizer need not have zero gradient; only feasible\ndirections are tested.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Unconstrained and unique cases", "role": "<p>Test the negative gradient as a direction, and use a midpoint to rule\nout two distinct minimizers. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>,\nzero gradient is equivalent to optimality; strict convexity gives at\nmost one minimizer.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E2/v1, and strict convexity when asserting uniqueness. Incoming proof\nexports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>,\nzero gradient is equivalent to optimality; strict convexity gives at\nmost one minimizer.</p>", "gate": "<p>Uniqueness does not imply existence; for example a function on an\nopen feasible set can have an unattained infimum.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a unique minimizer is declared without an existence argument,\nretain the precise at-most-one conclusion. Withhold this export and\nrecheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>In the unconstrained case substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=x_*-\\nabla f(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin E2 to get\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\|\\nabla f(x_*)\\|^2\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence the gradient is zero. The converse follows immediately from\nE2.</p>", "<p>If distinct\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*,z_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nboth minimize and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis strictly convex on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntheir midpoint lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has strictly smaller value than the average of their equal minimum\nvalues, a contradiction. This proves at-most-one, completing the\ntheorem.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>,\nzero gradient is equivalent to optimality; strict convexity gives at\nmost one minimizer.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E2/v1, and strict convexity when asserting uniqueness. Incoming proof\nexports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import\nversions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Test the negative gradient as a direction, and use a midpoint to rule\nout two distinct minimizers.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Uniqueness does not imply existence; for example a function on an\nopen feasible set can have an unattained infimum.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.2", "gate": "<p>E1/v1, convex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: A boundary minimizer need not have zero gradient; only feasible\ndirections are tested.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E2/v1, and strict convexity when asserting uniqueness. Check:\nUniqueness does not imply existence; for example a function on an open\nfeasible set can have an unattained infimum.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-build-the-supporting-inequality-1\">N1 — Build the supporting\ninequality</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;t\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nconvexity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x+t(y-x))-f(x)\\le t(f(y)-f(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDivide by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Differentiability at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nmakes the left quotient tend to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\downarrow0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRearrangement yields the supporting inequality for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-certify-constrained-optimality-1\">N2 — Certify constrained\noptimality</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nminimizes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe segment\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*+t(y-x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nremains feasible. Its difference quotient from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonnegative for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking the limit gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),y-x_*\\rangle\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Conversely, if those inequalities hold, E1\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x_*)+\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),y-x_*\\rangle\\ge f(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis is the required global conclusion.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-unconstrained-and-unique-cases-1\">N3 — Unconstrained and\nunique cases</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> In the unconstrained case substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=x_*-\\nabla f(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin E2 to get\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\|\\nabla f(x_*)\\|^2\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence the gradient is zero. The converse follows immediately from\nE2.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> If distinct\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*,z_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nboth minimize and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis strictly convex on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntheir midpoint lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has strictly smaller value than the average of their equal minimum\nvalues, a contradiction. This proves at-most-one, completing the\ntheorem.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=(x+1)^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=[0,\\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot zero, but\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(0)(y-0)=2y\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all feasible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe theorem certifies the boundary minimizer; strict convexity makes it\nunique.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Without convexity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nzero gradient need not indicate a minimum:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=-x^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a strict maximum at zero. Existence also fails for the strictly\nconvex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^2</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose infimum is not attained.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 claim:</strong> a constrained optimum must\nsatisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe worked boundary example refutes it. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong>\nIntellect tested infeasible negative directions.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> test only\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y-x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in C</annotation></semantics></math>\nand prove the variational inequality. This replaces the invalid\ncandidate with the exact §1 statement; the unconstrained zero-gradient\ncorollary still holds separately.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Add normal cones or convex inequality constraints to\ndevelop constrained optimality without confusing boundary points with\nunconstrained stationary points.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/\">Boyd and\nVandenberghe, Convex Optimization</a> for convexity, optimality, and\ndescent; <a\nhref=\"https://www.math.umd.edu/~mariakc/Spring2020Class.html\">University\nof Maryland, Scientific Computing I</a> for the numerical-analysis\nsetting. The estimates used here are derived explicitly in §4.</p>", "sha256": "1463c3033bf7066512230e38ddfeea69116789206ed8534313f5cc3c17d48c90", "pdf": "reports/pdf/first-order-convex-optimality.pdf"}, {"id": "ON-02", "slug": "lagrange-multiplier-theorem", "title": "Lagrange Multipliers under the Full-Rank Condition", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>The rank condition makes every vector in the linearized constraint\nkernel the velocity of an actual feasible curve. Stationarity along\nthose curves forces the gradient into the constraint row space.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:U\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h:U\\to\\mathbb R^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\non open\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\subset\\mathbb R^d</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le m&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSuppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x_*)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Dh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a local extremum of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nProve there is a unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=Dh(x_*)^T\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis is a necessary condition, not a general sufficient condition.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import the implicit function theorem: an invertible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\times m</annotation></semantics></math>\ncoordinate block of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Dh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives a local\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nparametrization of the zero set as a graph, whose derivative is obtained\nby differentiating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nUse the chain rule and finite-dimensional linear algebra: the row space\nof a full-row-rank matrix\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis identity follows from containment plus dimensions\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\non both sides.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Realize tangent directions by curves", "role": "<p>Use the implicit graph to convert a linearized feasible direction\ninto a genuinely feasible curve. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> For\nevery\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>\nthere is a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfeasible curve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma&#39;(0)=v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Dh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nof rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>\nthere is a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfeasible curve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma&#39;(0)=v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The invertible coordinate block is guaranteed by rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>;\nwithout it, the kernel may overestimate actual tangent directions.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a kernel vector is declared tangent without a feasible curve,\nconstruct it through the implicit graph and check the full-rank\nhypothesis. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>After permuting coordinates write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathbb R^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D_yh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\ninvertible. The implicit function theorem writes nearby feasible points\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\phi(z),z)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi(z_*)=y_*</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDifferentiating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(\\phi(z),z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\phi(z_*)=-(D_yh)^{-1}D_zh</annotation></semantics></math>,\nall derivatives evaluated at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v=(v_y,v_z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe equation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsays\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_y=D\\phi(z_*)v_z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma(t)=(\\phi(z_*+tv_z),z_*+tv_z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis feasible for small positive and negative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>,\npasses through\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand has derivative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>\nthere is a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfeasible curve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma&#39;(0)=v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Dh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\nof rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use the implicit graph to convert a linearized feasible direction\ninto a genuinely feasible curve.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The invertible coordinate block is guaranteed by rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>;\nwithout it, the kernel may overestimate actual tangent directions.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Annihilate the tangent space", "role": "<p>Differentiate the objective along each two-sided feasible curve.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)\\in(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and local constrained extremality. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)\\in(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Both signs of the curve parameter are available locally, allowing a\nzero derivative rather than a one-sided inequality.</p>", "repair": "<p>If an ambient extremum is assumed instead of a constrained one, apply\nstationarity only to the feasible curves already constructed. Withhold\nthis export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose the curve from E1. The scalar\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfunction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto f(\\gamma(t))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a local extremum at the interior parameter value zero. Its\nderivative is therefore zero.</p>", "<p>The chain rule gives that derivative as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),v\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>\nwas arbitrary in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe gradient annihilates that kernel.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)\\in(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and local constrained extremality. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Differentiate the objective along each two-sided feasible curve.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Both signs of the curve parameter are available locally, allowing a\nzero derivative rather than a one-sided inequality.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Recover and identify the multiplier", "role": "<p>Identify the orthogonal complement of the kernel with the image of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong> There is a unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=A^T\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E2/v1 and rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>There is a unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=A^T\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Uniqueness of the multiplier uses injectivity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot uniqueness of the constrained optimum.</p>", "repair": "<p>If multiplier existence is treated as sufficient for optimality,\nretain only the necessary condition and perform a separate second-order\nor convexity analysis. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants\nafter a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle A^T\\lambda,v\\rangle=\\langle\\lambda,Av\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}A^T\\subset(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe two spaces have dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving equality. E2 therefore supplies a multiplier.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T\\lambda=A^T\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T(\\lambda-\\mu)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFull row rank makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>\ninjective, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNo conclusion that every multiplier solution is an extremum has been\nused.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is a\nunique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=A^T\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E2/v1 and rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Identify the orthogonal complement of the kernel with the image of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Uniqueness of the multiplier uses injectivity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot uniqueness of the constrained optimum.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and local constrained extremality. Check: Both signs of the\ncurve parameter are available locally, allowing a zero derivative rather\nthan a one-sided inequality.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E2/v1 and rank\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: Uniqueness of the multiplier uses injectivity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot uniqueness of the constrained optimum.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-realize-tangent-directions-by-curves-1\">N1 — Realize tangent\ndirections by curves</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> After permuting coordinates write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathbb R^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D_yh(x_*)</annotation></semantics></math>\ninvertible. The implicit function theorem writes nearby feasible points\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\phi(z),z)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi(z_*)=y_*</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDifferentiating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(\\phi(z),z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\phi(z_*)=-(D_yh)^{-1}D_zh</annotation></semantics></math>,\nall derivatives evaluated at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v=(v_y,v_z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe equation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsays\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_y=D\\phi(z_*)v_z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma(t)=(\\phi(z_*+tv_z),z_*+tv_z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis feasible for small positive and negative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>,\npasses through\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand has derivative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-annihilate-the-tangent-space-1\">N2 — Annihilate the tangent\nspace</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose the curve from E1. The scalar\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfunction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto f(\\gamma(t))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a local extremum at the interior parameter value zero. Its\nderivative is therefore zero.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> The chain rule gives that derivative as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle\\nabla f(x_*),v\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>\nwas arbitrary in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe gradient annihilates that kernel.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-recover-and-identify-the-multiplier-1\">N3 — Recover and\nidentify the multiplier</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker A</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle A^T\\lambda,v\\rangle=\\langle\\lambda,Av\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}A^T\\subset(\\ker A)^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe two spaces have dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving equality. E2 therefore supplies a multiplier.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T\\lambda=A^T\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T(\\lambda-\\mu)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFull row rank makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^T</annotation></semantics></math>\ninjective, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNo conclusion that every multiplier solution is an extremum has been\nused.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Minimize\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,y)=x^2+y^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nsubject to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x,y)=x+y-1=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe gradient equation is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(2x,2y)=\\lambda(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSubstituting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=1-x</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=2(x-1/2)^2+1/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nseparately verifying that this stationary point is the global\nminimum.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>If rank fails, take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,y)=x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x,y)=x^2+y^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe feasible set is the single point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich is both a constrained minimum and maximum, but\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f=(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Dh=(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso no multiplier exists. Sufficiency also fails: for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,y)=x^3</annotation></semantics></math>\nsubject to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe origin satisfies the multiplier equation but is not an extremum.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N1 inference:</strong> every vector in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker Dh</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the velocity of a feasible curve, without a rank condition. The\nsingle-point constraint has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker Dh=\\mathbb R^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nat zero but only zero feasible velocities. <strong>Repair:</strong>\ninvoke full rank and the implicit graph exactly as N1 does. The original\ntheorem is preserved; the rank-free extension is rejected. Recheck\ntangent annihilation and multiplier existence.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Develop second-order conditions on the tangent\nspace, explicitly separating necessary and sufficient tests.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/\">Boyd and\nVandenberghe, Convex Optimization</a> for convexity, optimality, and\ndescent; <a\nhref=\"https://www.math.umd.edu/~mariakc/Spring2020Class.html\">University\nof Maryland, Scientific Computing I</a> for the numerical-analysis\nsetting. The estimates used here are derived explicitly in §4.</p>", "sha256": "93d0f7f6898ec672a182e81a8a5917a41e137e76092da379129eaef940ffd771", "pdf": "reports/pdf/lagrange-multiplier-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "ON-03", "slug": "gradient-descent-linear-convergence", "title": "Linear Convergence of Gradient Descent", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>Smoothness turns a gradient step into a quantified decrease. Strong\nconvexity both guarantees an optimum and links the remaining objective\ngap to the gradient size.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly\nconvex, and have an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ngradient, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;\\mu\\le L</annotation></semantics></math>.\nStrong convexity here means\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(x)+\\langle\\nabla f(x),y-x\\rangle+(\\mu/2)\\|y-x\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nProve there is a unique minimizer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nand, for exact-arithmetic iterates\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=x_k-\\nabla f(x_k)/L</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x_k)-f(x_*)\\le(1-\\mu/L)^k(f(x_0)-f(x_*))</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_k\\to x_*</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInterpret the bound at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nas equality, including when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu=L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use the fundamental theorem of calculus along a segment,\nCauchy–Schwarz, and attainment of the minimum of a continuous function\non a compact set. The gradient Lipschitz property is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\nabla f(x)-\\nabla f(y)\\|\\le L\\|x-y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAll norms are Euclidean. The theorem concerns exact iterations and does\nnot certify rounding-error behavior.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Existence and the gap estimate", "role": "<p>Use a quadratic lower bound for coercivity, then minimize the\nquadratic support model. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> A unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)-f(x_*)\\le\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Strong convexity with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>A unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)-f(x_*)\\le\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The lower bound must grow at infinity; a merely convex function need\nnot attain its infimum.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the sign of the gradient-gap estimate is reversed, complete the\nsquare explicitly; the resulting bound is a lower bound on gradient size\nin terms of the gap. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants\nafter a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>The strong-convexity inequality at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(0)+\\langle\\nabla f(0),y\\rangle+(\\mu/2)\\|y\\|^2\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|y\\|\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose a ball outside which\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&gt;f(0)</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncompact attainment inside it gives a global minimizer. Differentiability\ngives zero gradient there. Strict convexity, which follows from strong\nconvexity, gives uniqueness (or apply the quadratic lower bound at\neither minimizer).</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g=\\nabla f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nstrong convexity at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x_*)\\ge f(x)+\\langle g,x_*-x\\rangle+(\\mu/2)\\|x_*-x\\|^2\\ge f(x)-\\|g\\|^2/(2\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>\nby completing the square. Rearrangement proves the gap estimate.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: A unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f(x_*)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)-f(x_*)\\le\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Strong convexity with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use a quadratic lower bound for coercivity, then minimize the\nquadratic support model.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The lower bound must grow at infinity; a merely convex function need\nnot attain its infimum.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Quantify one step of descent", "role": "<p>Integrate the gradient difference along a segment to derive the\ndescent lemma. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x-\\nabla f(x)/L)\\le f(x)-\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>An\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ngradient and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=-\\nabla f(x)/L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x-\\nabla f(x)/L)\\le f(x)-\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>\ncomes from integrating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nfrom zero to one; the step is exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If arbitrary positive step sizes are declared descending, retain the\nsmoothness quadratic term and verify its coefficient before choosing a\nstep. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For any vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe fundamental theorem gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x+s)-f(x)-\\langle\\nabla f(x),s\\rangle=\\int_0^1\\langle\\nabla f(x+ts)-\\nabla f(x),s\\rangle\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts absolute value is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_0^1 Lt\\|s\\|^2dt=(L/2)\\|s\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=-\\nabla f(x)/L</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe linear term is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/L</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the quadratic term is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2L)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving the claimed decrease.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x-\\nabla f(x)/L)\\le f(x)-\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>An\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ngradient and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=-\\nabla f(x)/L</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Integrate the gradient difference along a segment to derive the\ndescent lemma.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>\ncomes from integrating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nfrom zero to one; the step is exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Iterate the contraction", "role": "<p>Combine the gap-gradient inequality with one-step descent, then\ncontrol distance by strong convexity at the minimizer. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong> The stated geometric objective bound holds and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x_k-x_*\\|^2\\le2(f(x_k)-f(x_*))/\\mu\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1 for every iterate. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at\nN3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>The stated geometric objective bound holds and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x_k-x_*\\|^2\\le2(f(x_k)-f(x_*))/\\mu\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Objective convergence alone is not automatically convergence of\npoints; the quadratic growth estimate supplies that bridge.</p>", "repair": "<p>If point convergence is inferred solely from function values, insert\nthe positive quadratic growth bound with its factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu/2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_k=f(x_k)-f(x_*)\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nE2 and E1 give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_{k+1}\\le\\Delta_k-\\|\\nabla f(x_k)\\|^2/(2L)\\le(1-\\mu/L)\\Delta_k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInduction gives the geometric bound. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu=L</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe first step has gap zero and all later iterates are the\nminimizer.</p>", "<p>Strong convexity at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere the gradient is zero, gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_k\\ge(\\mu/2)\\|x_k-x_*\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe objective bound therefore implies convergence of the iterates\nthemselves. This completes the existence, rate, and convergence\nclaims.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: The stated\ngeometric objective bound holds and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x_k-x_*\\|^2\\le2(f(x_k)-f(x_*))/\\mu\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1 for every iterate. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at\nN3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import\nversions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Combine the gap-gradient inequality with one-step descent, then\ncontrol distance by strong convexity at the minimizer.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Objective convergence alone is not automatically convergence of\npoints; the quadratic growth estimate supplies that bridge.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-3", "source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1 for every iterate. Check: Objective convergence alone\nis not automatically convergence of points; the quadratic growth\nestimate supplies that bridge.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1 for every iterate. Check: Objective convergence alone\nis not automatically convergence of points; the quadratic growth\nestimate supplies that bridge.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-existence-and-the-gap-estimate-1\">N1 — Existence and the gap\nestimate</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> The strong-convexity inequality at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)\\ge f(0)+\\langle\\nabla f(0),y\\rangle+(\\mu/2)\\|y\\|^2\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|y\\|\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose a ball outside which\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&gt;f(0)</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncompact attainment inside it gives a global minimizer. Differentiability\ngives zero gradient there. Strict convexity, which follows from strong\nconvexity, gives uniqueness (or apply the quadratic lower bound at\neither minimizer).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g=\\nabla f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nstrong convexity at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=x_*</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x_*)\\ge f(x)+\\langle g,x_*-x\\rangle+(\\mu/2)\\|x_*-x\\|^2\\ge f(x)-\\|g\\|^2/(2\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>\nby completing the square. Rearrangement proves the gap\nestimate.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-quantify-one-step-of-descent-1\">N2 — Quantify one step of\ndescent</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For any vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe fundamental theorem gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x+s)-f(x)-\\langle\\nabla f(x),s\\rangle=\\int_0^1\\langle\\nabla f(x+ts)-\\nabla f(x),s\\rangle\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts absolute value is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_0^1 Lt\\|s\\|^2dt=(L/2)\\|s\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=-\\nabla f(x)/L</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe linear term is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/L</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the quadratic term is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\nabla f(x)\\|^2/(2L)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving the claimed decrease.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-iterate-the-contraction-1\">N3 — Iterate the contraction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_k=f(x_k)-f(x_*)\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nE2 and E1 give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∇</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_{k+1}\\le\\Delta_k-\\|\\nabla f(x_k)\\|^2/(2L)\\le(1-\\mu/L)\\Delta_k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInduction gives the geometric bound. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu=L</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe first step has gap zero and all later iterates are the\nminimizer.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> Strong convexity at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_*</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere the gradient is zero, gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta_k\\ge(\\mu/2)\\|x_k-x_*\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe objective bound therefore implies convergence of the iterates\nthemselves. This completes the existence, rate, and convergence\nclaims.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,y)=(x^2+4y^2)/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=4</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe iteration sends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(3x/4,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFrom\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe first objective drops from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">9/32</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbelow the certified upper bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(3/4)(5/2)=15/8</annotation></semantics></math>.\nLater the actual remaining gap shrinks by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">9/16</annotation></semantics></math>\nper step, so the theorem’s\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/4</annotation></semantics></math>\nfactor is conservative.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>An arbitrary large step fails even for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^2/2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWith step size\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe iteration is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=-2x_k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the objective grows by a factor of four unless\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe prescribed step and smoothness bound cannot be discarded.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N3 argument:</strong> decreasing objective values\nguarantee convergence to the unique optimum with a geometric rate.\nMonotone numbers alone provide neither conclusion.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Intellect omitted the quantitative\ngradient-gap bridge. <strong>Repair:</strong> use E1 to obtain the\nactual contraction factor and the strong-convexity distance estimate.\nThis completes the original theorem under its existing assumptions;\nrecheck both objective and point convergence.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Investigate accelerated methods or inexact gradients\nwith newly stated error bounds; do not transfer this exact-arithmetic\nrate unchanged.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/\">Boyd and\nVandenberghe, Convex Optimization</a> for convexity, optimality, and\ndescent; <a\nhref=\"https://www.math.umd.edu/~mariakc/Spring2020Class.html\">University\nof Maryland, Scientific Computing I</a> for the numerical-analysis\nsetting. The estimates used here are derived explicitly in §4.</p>", "sha256": "a658b3215e43f4c1c5d639654c1adf74050094a751aabbfc0622a3085236124e", "pdf": "reports/pdf/gradient-descent-linear-convergence.pdf"}, {"id": "ON-04", "slug": "newton-local-quadratic-convergence", "title": "Local Quadratic Convergence of Newton’s Method", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>Express the next error as an integral of derivative differences. The\nquadratic estimate then proves its own invariant neighborhood, avoiding\na circular assumption that all iterates remain near the root.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\non an open interval containing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\alpha-r,\\alpha+r]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(\\alpha)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSuppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(x)|\\ge m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;&#39;(x)|\\le M</annotation></semantics></math>\non that closed interval, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=Mr/(2m)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the interval, the exact Newton iteration\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=x_k-f(x_k)/f&#39;(x_k)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis well defined, stays in the interval, and converges to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_{k+1}-\\alpha|\\le (M/(2m))|x_k-\\alpha|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use the fundamental theorem of calculus and its estimate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(u)-f&#39;(v)|\\le M|u-v|</annotation></semantics></math>\non the interval, obtained by integrating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNo existence of a root is inferred from numerical residuals: the theorem\nassumes the root\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nand proves convergence near it. Every simple root has some neighborhood\nsatisfying these hypotheses by continuity and a sufficiently small\nradius.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Derive the exact error estimate", "role": "<p>Subtract the secant integral from the tangent term and bound the\nderivative variation. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(x)=x-f(x)/f&#39;(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|N(x)-\\alpha|\\le (M/(2m))|x-\\alpha|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in[\\alpha-r,\\alpha+r]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(\\alpha)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(x)=x-f(x)/f&#39;(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|N(x)-\\alpha|\\le (M/(2m))|x-\\alpha|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The denominator stays away from zero by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe entire integration segment stays in the stated interval.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a Taylor remainder is used without a bound over the whole segment,\nuse this integral identity with the explicit uniform bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=x-\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe fundamental theorem gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=\\int_\\alpha^x f&#39;(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(x)-\\alpha=[e f&#39;(x)-f(x)]/f&#39;(x)=\\bigl(\\int_\\alpha^x(f&#39;(x)-f&#39;(t))\\,dt\\bigr)/f&#39;(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The absolute numerator is at most the integral of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M|x-t|</annotation></semantics></math>\nalong the segment, namely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M|e|^2/2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDivide by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(x)|\\ge m</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain the error estimate. This remains valid for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&lt;\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nafter taking the absolute value of the oriented integral.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(x)=x-f(x)/f&#39;(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|N(x)-\\alpha|\\le (M/(2m))|x-\\alpha|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in[\\alpha-r,\\alpha+r]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(\\alpha)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Subtract the secant integral from the tangent term and bound the\nderivative variation.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The denominator stays away from zero by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe entire integration segment stays in the stated interval.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Close the invariant and convergence", "role": "<p>Inductively keep every error within the radius, then sum no errors at\nall: directly contract their magnitudes. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong> All iterates exist,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le q^k|x_0-\\alpha|\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the quadratic bound holds at every step.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=Mr/(2m)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>All iterates exist,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le q^k|x_0-\\alpha|\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the quadratic bound holds at every step.</p>", "gate": "<p>Proving the estimate at one point is insufficient unless its next\niterate stays where the hypotheses hold.</p>", "repair": "<p>If local convergence is concluded while the iterates may leave the\nneighborhood, choose and prove an invariant radius before repeating the\nestimate. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nE1 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_{k+1}-\\alpha|\\le(M/(2m))|x_k-\\alpha|^2\\le q|x_k-\\alpha|\\le qr&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>\n(with immediate equality to zero allowed). The initial point satisfies\nthe premise, so induction proves that every denominator is nonzero and\nevery iterate remains in the interval.</p>", "<p>The same estimate yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le q^k|x_0-\\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving convergence. At each step E1 supplies the stronger quadratic\nerror inequality. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe first step reaches the root exactly. Finally a simple root has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(\\alpha)|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncontinuity gives a neighborhood with a positive derivative bound,\nbounded\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand after shrinking the radius,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: All iterates\nexist,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le q^k|x_0-\\alpha|\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the quadratic bound holds at every step.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=Mr/(2m)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Inductively keep every error within the radius, then sum no errors at\nall: directly contract their magnitudes.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Proving the estimate at one point is insufficient unless its next\niterate stays where the hypotheses hold.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=Mr/(2m)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: Proving the estimate at one point is insufficient unless its next\niterate stays where the hypotheses hold.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-derive-the-exact-error-estimate-1\">N1 — Derive the exact\nerror estimate</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=x-\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe fundamental theorem gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=\\int_\\alpha^x f&#39;(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(x)-\\alpha=[e f&#39;(x)-f(x)]/f&#39;(x)=\\bigl(\\int_\\alpha^x(f&#39;(x)-f&#39;(t))\\,dt\\bigr)/f&#39;(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> The absolute numerator is at most the\nintegral of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M|x-t|</annotation></semantics></math>\nalong the segment, namely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M|e|^2/2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDivide by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(x)|\\ge m</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain the error estimate. This remains valid for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&lt;\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nafter taking the absolute value of the oriented integral.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-close-the-invariant-and-convergence-1\">N2 — Close the\ninvariant and convergence</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nE1 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_{k+1}-\\alpha|\\le(M/(2m))|x_k-\\alpha|^2\\le q|x_k-\\alpha|\\le qr&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>\n(with immediate equality to zero allowed). The initial point satisfies\nthe premise, so induction proves that every denominator is nonzero and\nevery iterate remains in the interval.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> The same estimate yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x_k-\\alpha|\\le q^k|x_0-\\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving convergence. At each step E1 supplies the stronger quadratic\nerror inequality. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe first step reaches the root exactly. Finally a simple root has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(\\alpha)|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncontinuity gives a neighborhood with a positive derivative bound,\nbounded\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand after shrinking the radius,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^2-2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha=\\sqrt2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=1/4</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn that interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;|\\ge2(\\sqrt2-1/4)&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>\nis valid;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=1/8</annotation></semantics></math>.\nStarting at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0=3/2</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_1=17/12</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>577</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>408</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_2=577/408</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe exact identity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}-\\sqrt2=(x_k-\\sqrt2)^2/(2x_k)</annotation></semantics></math>\ndisplays the quadratic mechanism.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>At the multiple root of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nNewton gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=x_k/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_k\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nonly linear convergence. The derivative lower bound fails in every\nneighborhood of zero. Starting far away can also break local\nconvergence; this theorem does not promise a global basin.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 claim:</strong> the quadratic error formula\nproves convergence from every initial guess. <strong>Sense:</strong> its\nconstants were established only on a fixed interval, and outside it the\ndenominator may vanish. <strong>Repair:</strong> prove the radius\ninvariant using\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>\nbefore iteration. This supplies the missing step for the stated local\ntheorem; it does not extend the theorem globally. Recheck each use of E1\nalong the orbit.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Extend the argument to vector Newton methods using\nan invertible Jacobian and a controlled inverse, with explicit matrix\nnorm bounds.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/\">Boyd and\nVandenberghe, Convex Optimization</a> for convexity, optimality, and\ndescent; <a\nhref=\"https://www.math.umd.edu/~mariakc/Spring2020Class.html\">University\nof Maryland, Scientific Computing I</a> for the numerical-analysis\nsetting. The estimates used here are derived explicitly in §4.</p>", "sha256": "97702bacfb5aa133470b4d965d0a9a52b1c6c8c92f6358352427e0c6a748bac6", "pdf": "reports/pdf/newton-local-quadratic-convergence.pdf"}, {"id": "ON-05", "slug": "composite-trapezoidal-error", "title": "Composite Trapezoidal Rule with a Certified Error Bound", "level": "Introductory", "idea": "<p>A nonnegative kernel expresses the local quadrature error exactly.\nIts integral gives the constant, and summing local errors gives the\nglobal order.</p>", "target": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in C^2([a,b])</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=(b-a)/N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_j=a+jh</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDefine\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N=h(f(a)/2+\\sum_{j=1}^{N-1}f(x_j)+f(b)/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nProve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|T_N-\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx|\\le (b-a)h^2\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty/12</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nalso prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N\\ge\\int_a^b f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese concern exact sampled values and arithmetic.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use integration by parts for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nfunctions and finite sums. The bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nis finite by continuity on the compact interval. Distinguish quadrature\nerror from errors in function evaluation or floating-point summation,\nwhich require separate estimates.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Derive the one-panel kernel", "role": "<p>Integrate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Kf&#39;&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>\ntwice by parts to recover endpoint weights and the exact integral.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac h2(f(u)+f(v))-\\int_u^v f=\\int_u^v K(t)f&#39;&#39;(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>One interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math>\nof length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(t)=(t-u)(v-t)/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac h2(f(u)+f(v))-\\int_u^v f=\\int_u^v K(t)f&#39;&#39;(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The boundary values are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(u)=K(v)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;(u)=h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;(v)=-h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;&#39;=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the sign of the error is uncertain, recompute the endpoint\nderivatives of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nbefore taking absolute values. Withhold this export and recheck its\ndescendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Integration by parts gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_u^v Kf&#39;&#39;=-\\int_u^v K&#39;f&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at the endpoints. Integrating again gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-[K&#39;f]_u^v+\\int_u^v K&#39;&#39;f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Using the displayed endpoint derivatives and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;&#39;=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(h/2)(f(u)+f(v))-\\int_u^v f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the local error with the sign\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T-I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand, after setting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=t-u</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_u^v K=\\frac12\\int_0^h s(h-s)\\,ds=h^3/12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac h2(f(u)+f(v))-\\int_u^v f=\\int_u^v K(t)f&#39;&#39;(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>One interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math>\nof length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(t)=(t-u)(v-t)/2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Integrate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Kf&#39;&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>\ntwice by parts to recover endpoint weights and the exact integral.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The boundary values are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(u)=K(v)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;(u)=h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;(v)=-h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;&#39;=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Sum the error and certify convergence", "role": "<p>Add exact identities, then use nonnegativity of the kernel for\nmagnitude and sign. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> The stated\nabsolute error and convex-function overestimate hold; in particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N\\to\\int_a^b f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 on each of the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nequal panels. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>The stated absolute error and convex-function overestimate hold; in\nparticular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N\\to\\int_a^b f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=(b-a)/h</annotation></semantics></math>\npanels, so the local\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^3</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound becomes a global\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the local\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^3</annotation></semantics></math>\nrate is reported as the global rate, multiply by the number of panels\nand restore the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Summing the one-panel trapezoids counts each interior sample twice\nwith weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproducing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe exact error is the sum of the panel kernel integrals. Its absolute\nvalue is bounded by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(h^3/12)\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty=(b-a)h^2\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty/12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nevery kernel integral is nonnegative, proving the overestimate. Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe absolute bound also proves convergence. The smoothness and fixed\ninterval make the same derivative bound valid for all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: The stated\nabsolute error and convex-function overestimate hold; in particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N\\to\\int_a^b f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 on each of the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nequal panels. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated\nassumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Add exact identities, then use nonnegativity of the kernel for\nmagnitude and sign.</p>", "Sense": "<p>There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=(b-a)/h</annotation></semantics></math>\npanels, so the local\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^3</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound becomes a global\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 on each of the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nequal panels. Check: There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=(b-a)/h</annotation></semantics></math>\npanels, so the local\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^3</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound becomes a global\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-derive-the-one-panel-kernel-1\">N1 — Derive the one-panel\nkernel</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Integration by parts gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_u^v Kf&#39;&#39;=-\\int_u^v K&#39;f&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at the endpoints. Integrating again gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-[K&#39;f]_u^v+\\int_u^v K&#39;&#39;f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Using the displayed endpoint derivatives\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K&#39;&#39;=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(h/2)(f(u)+f(v))-\\int_u^v f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the local error with the sign\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T-I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand, after setting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=t-u</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_u^v K=\\frac12\\int_0^h s(h-s)\\,ds=h^3/12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-sum-the-error-and-certify-convergence-1\">N2 — Sum the error\nand certify convergence</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Summing the one-panel trapezoids counts\neach interior sample twice with weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproducing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_N</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe exact error is the sum of the panel kernel integrals. Its absolute\nvalue is bounded by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>∞</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(h^3/12)\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty=(b-a)h^2\\|f&#39;&#39;\\|_\\infty/12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nevery kernel integral is nonnegative, proving the overestimate. Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\to0</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe absolute bound also proves convergence. The smoothness and fixed\ninterval make the same derivative bound valid for all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^2</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_2=\\tfrac12(0+\\tfrac14+\\tfrac12)=3/8</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile the integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/3</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe error is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/24</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\cdot(1/2)^2\\cdot2/12=1/24</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConvexity correctly predicts an overestimate.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=|x|</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe one-panel trapezoid is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlthough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\naway from zero, the function is not\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^2</annotation></semantics></math>;\ntreating its a.e. second derivative as a classical uniform bound would\nincorrectly predict zero error.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N1 shortcut:</strong> use\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nalmost everywhere in the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nkernel formula for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x|</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Memory silently replaced classical\nregularity by an a.e. derivative without the needed absolute-continuity\nbridge. <strong>Repair:</strong> keep the stated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nhypothesis; for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsplit at its corner and integrate the two affine pieces separately,\nobtaining the exact value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThat split is a separate valid computation, not a proof of the\nunqualified bound.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Develop adaptive panel selection from local\nderivative bounds, then add explicit evaluation and roundoff error terms\nfor numerical certification.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/cvxbook/\">Boyd and\nVandenberghe, Convex Optimization</a> for convexity, optimality, and\ndescent; <a\nhref=\"https://www.math.umd.edu/~mariakc/Spring2020Class.html\">University\nof Maryland, Scientific Computing I</a> for the numerical-analysis\nsetting. The estimates used here are derived explicitly in §4.</p>", "sha256": "fef51be5b76992ab5043ea218b5efaaf38f3f1a88a82ab3364b3981e027f5613", "pdf": "reports/pdf/composite-trapezoidal-error.pdf"}], "links": [], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs relative to declared imports; no agent execution or formal verification claimed."};
